         *           ~ memory_get_usage() 
         *           ~ memory_get_usage(true) 
         *           ~ sys_getloadavg() 
         *
         * 'usage' - TTL-Records current CPU and memory 
         *           performance metrics. Return a 
         *           system performance report 
         *           ARRAY data structure with: 
         *           ~ current performance (now) 
         *           ~ hist performance @ TTL0=10s/10s 
         *           ~ hist performance @ TTL1=30s/0.5min 
         *           ~ hist performance @ TTL2=300s/5min 
         *           ~ hist performance @ TTL3=600s/10min 
         *           ~ hist performance @ TTL4=1800s/30min 
         *           ~ hist performance @ TTL5=3600s/1h 
         *           ~ hist performance @ TTL6=7200s/2h 
         *           ~ hist performance @ TTL7=14400s/4h 
         *           ~ hist performance @ TTL8=28800s/8h 
         *
         * 'delta' - TTL-Records current CPU and memory 
         *           performance metrics. Calculate 
         *           delta-performance from between an
         *           admin configurable start(0)-and-
         *           28800-secs vs current CPU and 
         *           memory telemetry and return a 
         *           system performance report 
         *           ARRAY data structure with: 
         *           ~ current performance (now) 
         *           ~ current performance: 
         *             --delta from Start 
         *             --delta from TTL0=10s/10s 
         *             --delta from TTL1=30s/0.5min 
         *             --delta from TTL2=300s/5min 
         *             --delta from TTL3=600s/10min 
         *             --delta from TTL4=1800s/30min 
         *             --delta from TTL5=3600s/1h 
         *             --delta from TTL6=7200s/2h 
         *             --delta from TTL7=14400s/4h 
         *             --delta from TTL8=28800s/8h 
         *
         * 'history' - TTL-Records current CPU and memory 
         *             performance metrics.
         *
         * Please Note: Although still experimental, 
         *              TTL-Recording current CPU and 
         *              memory performance metrics 
         *              with an appropriate TTL expire 
         *              regime on the reporting data 
         *              (the TTL expire is mainly for 
         *              when the reporting data sits 
         *              in SESSION under byte 
         *              restricted access control. 
         *              Otherwise, call it "Purge 
         *              reporting cache tables? Y/n:") 
         *              can be analyzed for learnings
         *              which effectively provide 
         *              visibility into the future. 
         *              And we cannot forget that at 
         *              the same time we collect this
         *              data, we are also contributing 
         *              to the server's running 
         *              processes, even the server's 
         *              total over all load and thus 
         *              it's real-time resource 
         *              management policies that we 
         *              are supporting by asking for 
         *              performance metrics. 
         *              And once we implement our 
         *              SESSION tables (when no one 
         *              loses session data anymore), 
         *              these TTL performance reports 
         *              stored in the data base...: 
         *              0 - 0s, 
         *              1 - 10s, 
         *              2 - 30s (0.5 min), 
         *              3 - 300s (5 min), 
         *              4 - 600s (10 min), 
         *              5 - 1800s (30 min), 
         *              6 - 3600s (1h), 
         *              7 - 7200s (2h),
         *              8 - 18000s (5h),
         *              9 - 28800s (8h)
         *
         * Where the cache 
         * ARRAY-structure-to-
         * PHP-NATIVE-function-output 
         * for 'history' is 
