                    You can put 4,294,967,295 files into a 
                    single folder if drive is formatted with 
                    NTFS (would be unusual if it were not) as 
                    long as you do not exceed 256 terabytes 
                    (single file size and space) or all of 
                    disk space that was available whichever 
                    is less.

                    For older FAT32 drives the limits are 
                    65,534 files in a single folder and max 
                    file size of 4 Gigabytes and 2TB of total 
                    space or all of disk space that was 
                    available or whichever is less.

